A||N||5||Marc Harris||Stock Plastic Vacuum Lines||||1||
Z||000000||Marc Harris||11-26-2001||12:32 AM||||I want to put the stock, premolded plastic vacuum lines back into my '87 4cyl.  The two I'm most interested in are the EGR-to-TBI and the MAP-to-TBI. Does anyone know if they're available?  Thanks!<P>Marc Harris<BR>San Jose, CA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-26-2001||10:11 AM||||I dunno if you can get them anymore from the dealer, but you could probably find some of off a junked car that aren't cracked.  Lots of GM cars used the 2.5  Just be careful handling them so they don't crack on you!  Or just buy some bulk tubing the same size and replace them that way.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||11-26-2001||10:37 AM||||Those lines shouldn't be hard to find in a salvage yard. If not, if you can salvage the rubber ends, some black pressure line for air shocks will work. You can heat it with a heat gun and mold it in whatever shape you need. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIERO JOHN-WI||11-26-2001||11:22 AM||||Rodney Dickman, makes them pre-bent in metal you just have to put your ends on them from your original lines.  I know he makes them for the V6 you'll have to ask him if he makes the 4 cylinder!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||revin||11-26-2001||11:39 AM||||best bet is the steel ones from rodney Dickson! last longer<P>------------------<BR>Revin||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-26-2001||07:30 PM||||I don't think rodney makes lines for the 4 cyl.<P>If the rubber ends are good... you can get the line material new at many parts stores. I got some at an Advance Auto. (Check partsamerica.com for the complete list of stores in that group.)<P>If the ends are bad... You'll need to scarf replacement rubber parts from junk cars, doesn't need to be Fiero. I've yet to find all the ends in a parts store. They might be in the MotorMite master catalog.<P>The plastic line forms when warmed. <P>I ran a very short nearly straight line to my MAP and used the line almost as it came for the EGR. (I straigtened a few inches in the middle of the EGR.)<P>Don't worry about duplicating the line exactly. Especially for the MAP. the shorter the MAP line is the better.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
